.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Jul 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-wallets-balances - Read a wallet's live on-chain balances (by id or 0x address)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 wallets balances  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a wallet's live on-chain balances across the configured chains.

.PP
Each chain reports the native gas-token balance and the active token balances,
or an error if that chain's RPC was unreachable (reported per chain, so one dead
RPC never hides the others). Use --chain-id / --symbol to narrow the result.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--chain-id\fP=0
	Restrict to one chain id

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for balances

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--symbol\fP=""
	Restrict tokens to this symbol, e.g. USDC (alias: --token)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 wallets balances 0xABCD… --chain-id 84532 --symbol USDC
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-wallets(1)\fP
